# Fix Export & Storage Crisis — Implementation Plan

## Updated Root Cause (Confirmed)

The 417 MB export has **ZERO images**. The entire 417 MB is **Isar pre-allocated empty space** being copied verbatim.

| What's happening | Actual Data | File on Disk | Waste |
|---|---|---|---|
| Isar `copyToFile()` | ~5-10 MB of records | **417 MB** pre-allocated file | **98% empty** |
| 4 Checkpoints | Same ~5-10 MB copied | **4 × 417 MB = 1.67 GB** | **99% empty** |
| Total on disk | **~10 MB of real data** | **1.27 GB** | **99.2% waste** |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The fix is clear: **Stop exporting the raw Isar file. Export the actual data as JSON instead.**

---

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> **Backward Compatibility**: Existing `.tahir` backup files (v1 format with raw Isar) will still be importable. 
> New exports will use v2 format (JSON + media). The import function will auto-detect the format.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Checkpoint Impact**: Reducing checkpoints from 4→2 and adding a change guard will NOT lose any data.
> Checkpoints are safety snapshots only — the primary database is always intact. Users can still restore from the 2 most recent checkpoints.

