### Phase 4: Memory-Safe Export (Prevents RAM crash)

#### [MODIFY] [backup_service.dart](file:///c:/Users/Moazzam%20Samoo/Desktop/Tahir%20Showroom/lib/app/core/services/backup_service.dart)

Since Phase 1 already makes the data tiny (~1 MB JSON), the main memory concern is media files at scale. The fix:

1. **Write ZIP file progressively** instead of building entire archive in memory
2. **Stream media files** one at a time into the ZIP

```dart
// Instead of:
final archive = Archive();
// ... add everything to memory ...
final zipData = ZipEncoder().encode(archive);  // ALL in RAM!
await outputFile.writeAsBytes(zipData);         // Write from RAM

// Do:
final encoder = ZipFileEncoder();
encoder.create(savePath);
encoder.addFile(dataJsonFile, 'data.json');     // Stream from disk
encoder.addFile(manifestFile, 'manifest.json');

// Stream each media file individually (never all in RAM)
if (await mediaDir.exists()) {
  final files = mediaDir.listSync(recursive: true).whereType<File>();
  for (final file in files) {
    final relativePath = p.relative(file.path, from: mediaDir.path);
    encoder.addFile(file, 'media/$relativePath');
  }
}
encoder.close();
```

> [!NOTE]
> The `archive` package may need to be supplemented with `dart:io` ZipFile support, or we can use the `ZipEncoder` with chunked writes. Will determine exact API during implementation.

