### Phase 5: Historical Media Batch Compression (Retroactive Optimization)

Currently, the 456 MB historical V1 backup contains high-resolution (uncompressed) images. When imported, these images are extracted to the `TahirShowroom/Media/` directory at their original massive sizes. Phase 3 only compresses *newly* added images. To shrink the size of existing files from the 456 MB database, we need a one-time migration tool.

**Goal**: Batch process the entire existing `Media` directory, applying the new compression logic to all historical image files, overwriting them.

#### [MODIFY] [file_service.dart](file:///c:/Users/Moazzam%20Samoo/Desktop/Tahir%20Showroom/lib/app/core/services/file_service.dart)
Add a public method `compressHistoricalMedia()` to handle the batch processing:
```dart
Future<void> compressHistoricalMedia({
  void Function(int total, int processed)? onProgress,
}) async {
  final mediaDir = await _getMediaDir();
  if (!await mediaDir.exists()) return;

  final files = mediaDir.listSync(recursive: true).whereType<File>().toList();
  // Filter for common image extensions (case-insensitive)
  final imageFiles = files.where((f) {
    final ext = p.extension(f.path).toLowerCase();
    return ext == '.jpg' || ext == '.jpeg' || ext == '.png' || ext == '.webp';
  }).toList();

  int processed = 0;
  for (final file in imageFiles) {
    // Reuse existing _compressImage helper
    // Temporarily save compressed file, then overwrite original
    final compressedFile = await _compressImage(file); 
    
    // If _compressImage actually modified the file (returned a new path)
    if (compressedFile.path != file.path) {
      await file.delete();
      await compressedFile.rename(file.path);
    }
    
    processed++;
    if (onProgress != null) onProgress(imageFiles.length, processed);
  }
}
```

