## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1: JSON Checkpoints or keep Isar checkpoints?**
> Converting checkpoints to JSON (Phase 2 optional) saves massive disk space but changes the restore mechanism. Should we:
> - **Option A**: Keep Isar checkpoints but reduce to 2 + change guard (simple, safe)
> - **Option B**: Convert checkpoints to JSON too (maximum savings, more work)
> 
> **My recommendation**: Option A for now. It saves ~800 MB and is risk-free. We can convert to JSON checkpoints later if needed.

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> **Q2: Should old v1 `.tahir` exports still be importable?**
> I plan to support both formats (auto-detect on import). But if you never want to support old exports, we can simplify the code. **My recommendation**: Keep backward compatibility.

